# What the image is built from: an ALLOW list of the tracked top-level entries of web/, nothing else. The web and celery containers can create new
# files in the host's web/ folder (the update channel: .update-approved and the other request files, docs/UPDATES.md), but never change or rename one
# that is not theirs (the folder has the sticky bit, see web/ownership.sh). A name that is not on this list, such as a module planted there, is
# therefore never copied into the next image, and neither are the secret, .commit or the .update-* files. A new top-level file or folder in web/
# needs its line here (tests/test_image_user.py checks the list against git).
*
!.version
!.edition
!Dockerfile
!agentapi
!art
!beat-entrypoint.sh
!celery-entrypoint.sh
!celery_healthcheck.py
!cveFeed
!dashboard
!db-role.sh
!entrypoint.sh
!fixtures
!manage.py
!migrate-entrypoint.sh
!ownership.sh
!reNgine
!recon_note
!requirements.txt
!scanEngine
!startScan
!static
!targetApp
!templates
!tenancy
!tests
# never, even below an allowed folder
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
